WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.175
Lesson 2.4.

00:00:02.175 --> 00:00:05.320
Impermanent loss & true LP P&L.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.874
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:10.910
able to calculate an LP position's full P&L

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.395
and judge it against simply holding.

00:00:14.695 --> 00:00:15.985
Here's the plan.

00:00:15.985 --> 00:00:17.670
First, the key ideas.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:20.385
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:20.385 --> 00:00:21.910
Then, your checklist.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.072
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:25.372 --> 00:00:29.759
Impermanent loss (IL) is how much the LP

00:00:29.759 --> 00:00:35.536
position lags simply holding the same starting tokens

00:00:35.536 --> 00:00:40.244
when their relative price changes: IL = 2√r

00:00:40.244 --> 00:00:42.277
÷ (1 + r) − 1 (r =

00:00:42.277 --> 00:00:45.252
new price ÷ entry price).

00:00:45.252 --> 00:00:48.212
It's "impermanent" only if price returns.

00:00:48.212 --> 00:00:50.697
Withdraw after the move and it's permanent.

00:00:50.697 --> 00:00:53.810
Full LP P&L = LP value + fees

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:58.272
+ incentives − gas, compared to hold value.

00:00:59.572 --> 00:01:03.568
Deposit 1 ETH + 3,000 USDC

00:01:03.568 --> 00:01:08.457
at ETH = $3,000 (total $6,000).

00:01:08.457 --> 00:01:11.302
ETH rises to $4,000.

00:01:11.302 --> 00:01:14.610
A master judges the LP on

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:18.217
the +$58, not the +$1,058.

00:01:18.217 --> 00:01:24.122
Calculator: the calculator Starting $6,000: +$1,058 (mostly

00:01:24.122 --> 00:01:27.867
from ETH going up, not from LPing).

00:01:27.867 --> 00:01:32.122
Holding: +$58, the actual value added by LPing.

00:01:33.422 --> 00:01:37.022
Let's look at the chart: Impermanent loss vs holding.

00:01:37.022 --> 00:01:38.582
Take a moment with it.

00:01:38.582 --> 00:01:40.992
It's everything we've just said, in one picture.

00:01:42.292 --> 00:01:43.752
Here's your checklist.

00:01:43.752 --> 00:01:45.287
Do it now, for real.

00:01:45.287 --> 00:01:48.212
First, P&L tracked against hold, weekly.

00:01:48.212 --> 00:01:53.347
Next, IL, fees, incentives and gas recorded separately.

00:01:53.347 --> 00:01:55.395
And finally, Exit if fees

00:01:55.395 --> 00:01:57.758
consistently fail to cover IL.

00:01:59.058 --> 00:02:00.268
Question 1.

00:02:00.268 --> 00:02:01.833
ETH doubles.

00:02:01.833 --> 00:02:04.343
IL on a 50/50 pool?

00:02:08.763 --> 00:02:12.623
The answer: About −5.7% vs holding.

00:02:13.923 --> 00:02:15.168
Question 2.

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:18.443
Your LP is up 20% since deposit.

00:02:18.443 --> 00:02:19.528
Did LPing work?

00:02:23.948 --> 00:02:27.138
The answer: Unknown until you compare with holding.

00:02:27.138 --> 00:02:29.103
The 20% could be all price.

00:02:30.403 --> 00:02:31.673
Question 3.

00:02:31.673 --> 00:02:34.062
When does IL become permanent?

00:02:38.482 --> 00:02:40.593
The answer: When you withdraw while the

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.492
price ratio is different from entry.

00:02:43.793 --> 00:02:46.308
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:46.308 --> 00:02:51.072
Next up, Lesson 2.5: MEV and protecting your trades.
